  "explainLog": "One dot per day, sized by how long you trained that day. This week stops at today; last week shows all seven days.",
  "explainMainProgress": "Each point is one week's total, weeks starting on Monday. A week with nothing in it is still drawn at zero, so the axis stays evenly spaced. Switching the sport chip changes the chart and the three figures with it.",
  "explainMonthly": "Training time accumulated day by day. The bold line is this month and stops at today; the thin one is last month, drawn in full for comparison.",
  "explainPrediction": "Riegel's formula: a time over one distance predicts another, t2 = t1 × (d2/d1)^1.06. Only runs of 1.5 km or more in the last 30 days count. Each point is the best prediction so far, which is why the line only moves the faster way.",
  "explainRecords": "Your standing bests at the classic distances, read from each run's distance data. One current record per distance.",
  "explainStreak": "Consecutive weeks with at least one session, counted backwards. An empty current week does not break the streak — it has not happened yet.",
  "explainSuggestion": "Sized from your running volume over the last four weeks and how many days you have rested — not from a coaching plan. Trained yesterday means a recovery run; a weekend with enough volume behind it means a long one.",
  "explainZones": "Time in each heart-rate zone over the last 30 days, against the 30 days before that. There are numbers only when a session carried heart-rate data from a monitor.",
